-- EXPECT-ERROR: cannot verify precondition `_ > 0` on `need_pos`
-- A callback parameter's own refinement annotation is not a fact (2026-10-18,
-- found by the fold-accumulator invariants phase 1 guards): the demand
-- discharge checked the step's tail with `acc : {Int | _ > 100}` ASSUMED,
-- although nothing checks that annotation (the callee's domain is the type
-- variable `b`), so `acc - 50 > 0` proved and `cap verified` accepted this
-- module; `List.fold_left([5], 1, …)` is -49.  The annotation is now erased
-- there.  Since phase 4 it is read as the accumulator invariant and checked:
-- its base `1 > 100` fails, so it is still not assumed (its own obligation
-- is a second skip; reject/t451 and t452 pin that message).  A skip, an
-- error under `cap verified`.
mod FoldStepOwnAnnotationUnassumed do
  cap verified
  fn need_pos(k : {Int | _ > 0}) : Int do k end
  fn go(pos : List({Int | _ > 0})) : Int do
    need_pos(List.fold_left(pos, 1, fn (acc : {Int | _ > 100}, _x) -> acc - 50))
  end
end
